 ## Codebase Patterns
+- Kubernetes operations artifacts should be pinned by static release tests and an offline render path: keep `deploy/kubernetes/yalla-control-plane.yaml`, `deploy/kubernetes/README.md`, `deploy/kubernetes/kustomization.yaml`, SECURITY.md, CI, and `scripts/verify.sh` in lockstep; never check in Secret objects; bind runtime credentials from `yalla-control-plane-secrets`; preserve separate API/worker workloads and least-privilege pod security.
 - Success-envelope soft-limit alerts are structured `yalla.output.v1.warnings`, not endpoint `data`: emit them through `apienvelope.WriteDataWithWarnings` with stable codes plus `entitlement_key`, `usage`, `threshold`, `limit`, optional `period`, and recovery/upgrade `hint`; derive usage warnings only from already-authorized tenant-scoped rows so denied or cross-tenant responses never leak warning metadata.
 - Local Docker Compose is both a Postgres integration-test dependency stack and an opt-in `control-plane` operations profile: keep `postgres` profile-free with a pinned major image and healthcheck; put `yalla-api` and `yalla-worker` behind `profiles: [control-plane]`; build them from `Dockerfile` / `Dockerfile.worker`; require secret-shaped environment values through `${VAR:?message}` interpolation; wait on `postgres.condition=service_healthy`; harden API/worker services with `read_only: true`, `cap_drop: [ALL]`, `security_opt: [no-new-privileges:true]`, `/tmp` tmpfs, explicit JSON logging, and `restart: unless-stopped`; publish only the API's `8080:8080` for `/healthz` and `/readyz`.
 - Production worker container artifacts use a dedicated `Dockerfile.worker` rather than overloading the API image: keep the same distroless/nonroot/no-secrets hardening, build `./cmd/yalla-worker`, copy `/out/yalla-worker` to `/usr/local/bin/yalla-worker`, keep the entrypoint on that binary, document that the worker has no HTTP listener, and pin the contract through `internal/release/container_hardening_static_test.go` plus `SECURITY.md`.
